Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 01:33:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 424/488] [DS4.1] The sink detector's column from the last
 collapse

Every forward took the sink detector's column of the residual streams
with a strided cast copy and copied it into the detector's buffer. The
last collapse reads every stream anyway: its sink-column variant has the
thread holding that column write each stream's value as FP32, straight
into the buffer when every row is on this rank (gathered after
otherwise). Two kernels a step go; the collapse is unchanged bit for
bit. B12X's collapse takes the same arguments with a torch copy.
